/**
 * @page topic_socket Socket and Platform I/O
 * @ingroup module_abstractions
 * @brief Low-level socket helpers used inside transport implementations.
 *
 * Socket helpers provide cross-platform creation, addresses, timeouts,
 * nonblocking mode, send/receive, polling, and shutdown. They are infrastructure
 * for TCP, WebSocket, discovery probes, and other backends—not the application
 * protocol API.
 *
 * @section socket_boundary Boundary
 *
 * Application code should use `network_connection_t` and `acip_transport_t`.
 * Backend code may use the socket API to implement readiness, listener setup,
 * or interruption. A new feature belongs in the connection/transport contract
 * first, then in the platform socket implementation if needed.
 *
 * @section socket_lifecycle Lifecycle
 *
 * Resolve or construct an address, create the socket, set required options,
 * bind/connect/listen, and close it only after all users have stopped. A close
 * or shutdown must be able to interrupt blocked backend work without leaving
 * another thread holding a borrowed descriptor.
 *
 * @section socket_portability Portability
 *
 * POSIX and Windows differ in error values, readiness APIs, and how closing a
 * descriptor interrupts a blocked call. Keep those differences behind the
 * platform layer; callers consume `asciichat_error_t` and the shared socket
 * abstractions.
 *
 * @see topic_network
 * @see topic_platform
 */
